WEBVTT

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:03.880
SIEM should be viewed as one layer within a broader security program.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.560
It works alongside endpoint protection, EDR, vulnerability management, identity security,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.899
firewalls, cloud monitoring, incident response processes, and security awareness efforts.

00:00:12.899 --> 00:00:14.840
SIEM provides visibility and analysis,

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.980
helping organizations detect suspicious activity and investigate incidents more

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:19.740
efficiently.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.660
It does not stop every incident by itself,

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.080
and it does not make other controls unnecessary.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.660
Its value is strongest when it complements prevention, monitoring, response,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.400
and continuous improvement.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.019
When combined with skilled analysts and effective processes,

00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:34.800
SIEM becomes a valuable force multiplier for defenders.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.360
It helps teams turn raw logs into operational awareness, connect events across systems,

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.030
and make better decisions during investigation and response.
